Weights UX: sha256-verified auto-download, cache-dir default, env override

Implements the org Weights UX contract (constitution art. 4) for 0.1.4;
twin change with bs-roformer-infer 0.1.4.

- data/checksums.json records known-good sha256+size for all 71 assets whose
  URLs were live in the 2026-07-12 audit (53 checkpoints + 18 configs).
  Hashes from HF LFS pointers, cross-verified against local copies for
  MelBandRoformer.ckpt (two copies) and big_beta6.ckpt (one copy);
  download_file/verify_file_integrity now enforce them -- mismatch deletes
  the file and retries. get_file_hash() was dead code; it is now the actual
  verification path.
- melband-roformer-infer auto-resolves weights when
  --model_path/--config_path are omitted: new ensure_model_assets() looks up
  the model in the models dir and downloads (verified) on first use. New
  --model/--models_dir flags; explicit paths still win.
- Models dir defaults to ~/.cache/melband-roformer-infer/ (was CWD-relative
  ./models), overridable via MELBAND_ROFORMER_MODELS_PATH or CLI/API args;
  legacy ./models is still searched so existing downloads keep working.
- Version single-sourced from __about__.py (hatch dynamic); bumped to 0.1.4.
- README weights section rewritten to be truthful (auto-download, manual
  recipe with URL+sha256, folder override); availability note refreshed with
  the 2026-07-12 re-audit (37/89 fully usable, 36 checkpoints dead, 10 fully
  dead; inst_gaboxFv8[B].ckpt HF overrides also confirmed dead).
- tests/test_weights_ux.py: offline unit tests for hash verification wiring,
  models-dir resolution, and a live-override-has-checksum lock (18 new
  tests; suite 25 -> 43 green).
- ruff --fix removed two pre-existing extraneous f-string prefixes in
  download.py (parity with the twin's 0.1.2 cleanup).

No inference math touched.

