fix: repoint dead registry download URLs, incl. jarredou account deletion

Full liveness audit of every checkpoint/config URL melband's download
pipeline resolves to (121 unique URLs across 89 registry models) found 92
dead (404/401), most predating this session -- default-URL construction
(DEFAULT_CKPT_BASE_URL / DEFAULT_CONFIG_BASE_URL) guessing at filenames
that were never actually hosted at that generic path for most third-party
uploaders, not a single new regression.

One entry *is* the exact jarredou-account-deletion pattern the twin
bs-roformer-infer just hit: overrides.json's config_mel_band_roformer_karaoke.yaml
pointed at huggingface.co/jarredou/aufr33-viperx-karaoke-melroformer-model,
and the jarredou account is now fully gone (404 on the account page itself,
401 on the resolve URL).

Repointed 43 dead checkpoint/config entries to Politrees/UVR_resources, an
actively-maintained public HF mirror of the same UVR/roformer model set
(cross-referenced by exact/case-insensitive filename match against its file
tree, then HEAD-verified live with a plausible file size before adding).
This includes the jarredou-tainted config plus its paired dead checkpoint
(KaraokeGabox.ckpt), and a shared config
(config_mel_band_roformer_instrumental_gabox.yaml) that unblocks ~20 Gabox
instrumental-variant models at once.

Net effect: fully-broken models (both checkpoint and config dead) drop from
32 to 10; the DEFAULT_MODEL (melband-roformer-kim-vocals) was never
affected. The default model for every user was healthy throughout.

Remaining ~52 dead URLs (mostly Gabox instrumental/vocal checkpoint variants
that this mirror doesn't carry, plus a handful of others) could not be
matched to a live source with reasonable confidence within this session and
are left as-is rather than guessed at -- see the twin-sync campaign report
for the full per-model breakdown and a recommended follow-up.

